ed, and what the timer offers is a picture of its own window: LiveSplit's README says any run can be shared to Speedrun.com, X and Bluesky, and \\\"You can also share a screenshot of your splits to Imgur\\\".\",\n889-    \"The site that turned splits into something to look at is gone. LiveSplit issue #2543: splits.io shut down on March 31, 2025, and \\\"the splits for Speedrun.com runs were stored on Splits.io\\\". Its author: \\\"It always lost money as a side project.\\\"\",\n890-    \"Runners write their own tools on the .lss because \\\"LiveSplit files store a ton of very useful data\\\" and \\\"LiveSplit itself does not provide any built-in analytics features\\\" (LiveSplit-Analytics-Database; lss-tools does the same).\",\n891-  ],\n892-  sources: [\n893-    \"https://github.com/LiveSplit/LiveSplit\",\n894-    \"https://github.com/LiveSplit/LiveSplit/issues/2543\",\n895-    \"https://twos.dev/splitsio.html\",\n896-    \"https://github.com/JuanCruzCB/LiveSplit-Analytics-Database\",\n897-    \"https://github.com/slaurent22/lss-tools\",\n898-  ],\n899-  solution: [\n900-    \"The splits file is the prop. Paste a LiveSplit .lss into lss: the run is its Personal Best, the comparison the previous PB rebuilt from the attempt history, the golds its best segments. Or pass rows of { name, split, pb, best }. Deltas follow LiveSplit's own colour rule.\",\n901-    \"The clip opens on the finished recap, replays the run with a fast-forwarded timer as each split lands at its share of the run, and ends where it began, so it loops. The graph (portrait, landscape) is the time saved or lost on each segment. All moving text is gated drawtext: 16 rows cost two overlays.\",\n902-    \"Weak spots, honestly: no gameplay yet - the v2 is the same props over the recorded run at 1:1 - and the previous PB is only as good as the file's history.\",\n903-  ],\n904-  usage: {\n905-    command: \"m0saic make @one-a-day/gaming/speedrun-pb-recap/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1920 -o recap.mp4\"